Under Clause 1.1 of the Kenway NDA, “Confidential Information” is defined broadly as **all confidential information** disclosed by a Party or its Representatives, including but not limited to:

- the fact and status of discussions/negotiations concerning the Purpose;
- information relating to the **business, affairs, customers, clients, suppliers, plans, intentions, or market opportunities** of the Disclosing Party or its Group;
- information relating to the **operations, processes, product information, know-how, designs, specifications, trade secrets or software** of the Disclosing Party or its Group;
- any information or analysis derived from Confidential Information.

So technical information is included, but it is **not the only** type of Confidential Information covered by the agreement.

