rag_answer:
Yes. Under the Street Stream Franchise NDA, the Recipient (Receiving Party) may disclose Confidential Information to certain employees, but only if they qualify as “Authorised Persons” — i.e., employees engaged in respect of the Purpose — and only subject to the conditions in clause 3.

Specifically, the Recipient must:

- inform the employees beforehand of their confidentiality duties under the Agreement;
- ensure they undertake to comply with the same confidentiality obligations;
- keep a written record of each disclosure;
- notify the Disclosers immediately if an Authorised Person breaches the obligations; and
- provide evidence of compliance if requested by the Disclosers.

So, limited sharing with employees is permitted, but not unrestricted sharing.

